{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtPNMppCTasNjpigueDX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The usage log shows the problem clearly. After each `save_fact`, the next call has `cache_read_input_tokens: 0` and rewrites about 1,000–1,300 tokens. The cache breakpoint covers the whole system block, and that block includes the facts list. The static part is roughly 2,500 characters of instructions plus about 400 characters of tool schemas.\n\nThe naive fix is to split the block. But a split only helps if the static prefix still meets the model's minimum cacheable length, which for Sonnet 4.5 is 1,024 tokens. I can't count tokens exactly here without calling the API, so I'll keep the cached block as large as the design allows (instructions plus the stable profile) and put only the changing parts (facts and today's date) after the breakpoint. Then I'll check the result locally."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5929,"cache_read_input_tokens":28099,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5929},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35152304-2cef-414c-95df-0cd2163e95f5","uuid":"ce68267c-84db-4222-886b-ff9d29660e64","timestamp":"2026-11-10T01:33:52.111Z","request_id":"req_011CgtPNMe9xCf7tNXwirfcm"}
