{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtPRErCffwV1Z5A2aFTe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The test passes, and the repo's `data/` and `logs/` are untouched. Now I'll write ANSWER.md."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1406,"cache_read_input_tokens":41265,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1406},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35152304-2cef-414c-95df-0cd2163e95f5","uuid":"cb706ff7-7522-4861-a1f7-e5b9f1b6cf16","timestamp":"2026-11-10T01:34:20.610Z","request_id":"req_011CgtPREfnbNfRp8m4u5gtH"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtPRErCffwV1Z5A2aFTe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XMxjDXv467pfAC23nku8kj","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-BGIASR/ANSWER.md","content":"# Answer: save_fact evicts the cached system prompt\n\n## Cause\n\n`build_system()` put the whole system prompt in one text block with\n`cache_control`: the coaching instructions, the athlete profile, the date, and\nthe long-term facts list. The cache breakpoint covers everything up to and\nincluding that block, so any change to the block invalidates the cache. Every\n`save_fact` appends to `a.facts`, which changes the block. The next request\nthen reads 0 cached tokens and rewrites about 1,000–1,300 tokens at the cache\nwrite price. That matches `logs/usage.jsonl`: the call after each `save_fact`\nshows `cache_read_input_tokens: 0` and a large `cache_creation_input_tokens`.\n\nThe same thing happened inside a single message. `reply()` mutates `a` in\n`run_tool()`, and `build_request()` rebuilds the system prompt for round 2, so\nround 2 of a `save_fact` turn also missed the cache.\n\n## Change (`bot.py`)\n\nThe system prompt is now two text blocks:\n\n1. **Static block, cached** — `INSTRUCTIONS` plus the stable profile (name,\n   sport, zones, goal, language). It is byte-identical across `save_fact`\n   calls, across rounds of one message, and across days.\n2. **Dynamic block, not cached** — today's date and the facts list. It sits\n   after the cache breakpoint, so a memory write re-sends only this small\n   block at normal input price.\n\n`athlete_context()` was replaced by `profile_context()` and `facts_context()`.\n`build_system()` returns the two blocks. Nothing else changed: the tool\nselection, the logging, and the `save_fact` behaviour are the same.\n\n## Verification\n\nI ran `reply()` with a fake LLM (no API calls, and the athlete and usage files\nwere redirected to a temp directory, so `data/` and `logs/` were not modified):\n\n- Turn 1 saves a fact in a tool round. The cached block is identical in round 1,\n  round 2 and turn 2. The fact appears only in the uncached block.\n- The cached block is identical for 2026-11-09 and 2026-11-10.\n\nI have not checked this against the live API, and I did not deploy.\n\n## Open risk: the 1,024-token minimum\n\nPrompt caching only engages when the cached prefix reaches the model's minimum\n(1,024 tokens for Sonnet 4.5, the model in `bot.py`). The cached prefix is now\ntools + static block, about 3,050 characters. From the existing log, the old\nprefix (about 3,300 characters) was 1,000–1,300 tokens, which suggests the new\nprefix is only just over or just under 1,024. I could not count tokens exactly\nwithout calling the API, so I did not check it that way.\n\nIf the prefix is under the minimum, caching will not engage at all, and every\ncall will be billed at full input price. That would be worse than before for\nathletes whose facts were stable.\n\n**How to check after deploying:** in `logs/usage.jsonl`, a normal follow-up\nmessage should show `cache_read_input_tokens` near the static size, and\n`cache_creation_input_tokens` should be 0. If `cache_creation_input_tokens` and\n`cache_read_input_tokens` are both 0 for every call, the prefix is below the\nminimum. The fix would be to add about 100 tokens of stable content to the\nstatic block. Do not pad it with filler.\n\n## Not changed\n\n- **Tool selection changes the prefix.** `select_tools()` changes the `tools`\n  array, which comes before the system prompt in the cache order. A message\n  that switches tool sets (for example, a planning keyword) therefore misses\n  the cache even when the athlete's data is unchanged. NOTES.md says the\n  keyword filter was a clear win, so I left it. A possible follow-up is to\n  always send the full tool list and cache it.\n- The facts block is not cached. It is small, and caching it would cost a cache\n  write on every save, which is what we are trying to avoid.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1406,"cache_read_input_tokens":41265,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1406},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35152304-2cef-414c-95df-0cd2163e95f5","uuid":"80e0cff8-a48a-492f-a3d8-ed901f7bdb56","timestamp":"2026-11-10T01:34:26.598Z","request_id":"req_011CgtPREfnbNfRp8m4u5gtH","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XMxjDXv467pfAC23nku8kj":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-BGIASR/ANSWER.md","content":"# Answer: save_fact evicts the cached system prompt\n\n## Cause\n\n`build_system()` put the whole system prompt in one text block with\n`cache_control`: the coaching instructions, the athlete profile, the date, and\nthe long-term facts list. The cache breakpoint covers everything up to and\nincluding that block, so any change to the block invalidates the cache. Every\n`save_fact` appends to `a.facts`, which changes the block. The next request\nthen reads 0 cached tokens and rewrites about 1,000–1,300 tokens at the cache\nwrite price. That matches `logs/usage.jsonl`: the call after each `save_fact`\nshows `cache_read_input_tokens: 0` and a large `cache_creation_input_tokens`.\n\nThe same thing happened inside a single message. `reply()` mutates `a` in\n`run_tool()`, and `build_request()` rebuilds the system prompt for round 2, so\nround 2 of a `save_fact` turn also missed the cache.\n\n## Change (`bot.py`)\n\nThe system prompt is now two text blocks:\n\n1. **Static block, cached** — `INSTRUCTIONS` plus the stable profile (name,\n   sport, zones, goal, language). It is byte-identical across `save_fact`\n   calls, across rounds of one message, and across days.\n2. **Dynamic block, not cached** — today's date and the facts list. It sits\n   after the cache breakpoint, so a memory write re-sends only this small\n   block at normal input price.\n\n`athlete_context()` was replaced by `profile_context()` and `facts_context()`.\n`build_system()` returns the two blocks. Nothing else changed: the tool\nselection, the logging, and the `save_fact` behaviour are the same.\n\n## Verification\n\nI ran `reply()` with a fake LLM (no API calls, and the athlete and usage files\nwere redirected to a temp directory, so `data/` and `logs/` were not modified):\n\n- Turn 1 saves a fact in a tool round. The cached block is identical in round 1,\n  round 2 and turn 2. The fact appears only in the uncached block.\n- The cached block is identical for 2026-11-09 and 2026-11-10.\n\nI have not checked this against the live API, and I did not deploy.\n\n## Open risk: the 1,024-token minimum\n\nPrompt caching only engages when the cached prefix reaches the model's minimum\n(1,024 tokens for Sonnet 4.5, the model in `bot.py`). The cached prefix is now\ntools + static block, about 3,050 characters. From the existing log, the old\nprefix (about 3,300 characters) was 1,000–1,300 tokens, which suggests the new\nprefix is only just over or just under 1,024. I could not count tokens exactly\nwithout calling the API, so I did not check it that way.\n\nIf the prefix is under the minimum, caching will not engage at all, and every\ncall will be billed at full input price. That would be worse than before for\nathletes whose facts were stable.\n\n**How to check after deploying:** in `logs/usage.jsonl`, a normal follow-up\nmessage should show `cache_read_input_tokens` near the static size, and\n`cache_creation_input_tokens` should be 0. If `cache_creation_input_tokens` and\n`cache_read_input_tokens` are both 0 for every call, the prefix is below the\nminimum. The fix would be to add about 100 tokens of stable content to the\nstatic block. Do not pad it with filler.\n\n## Not changed\n\n- **Tool selection changes the prefix.** `select_tools()` changes the `tools`\n  array, which comes before the system prompt in the cache order. A message\n  that switches tool sets (for example, a planning keyword) therefore misses\n  the cache even when the athlete's data is unchanged. NOTES.md says the\n  keyword filter was a clear win, so I left it. A possible follow-up is to\n  always send the full tool list and cache it.\n- The facts block is not cached. It is small, and caching it would cost a cache\n  write on every save, which is what we are trying to avoid.\n"}}}
