{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtPSdRnv1u3K7geNnTny","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The system prompt is now split so a `save_fact` no longer evicts the cached instructions. I checked this with a fake LLM, not against the live API, and I didn't deploy anything.\n\n**Cause:** the whole system prompt was one cached block, and it included the facts list. Every `save_fact` changed the block, so the next call read 0 cached tokens and rewrote about 1,000–1,300 tokens. The same happened on round 2 of the message that saved the fact, because `reply()` rebuilt the prompt after the save.\n\n**Change in `bot.py`:**\n- **Cached block:** the coaching instructions plus the stable profile (name, sport, zones, goal, language). It stays byte-identical across `save_fact` calls, across rounds, and across days.\n- **Uncached block:** today's date and the facts list. It sits after the cache breakpoint, so a memory write only re-sends this small block.\n\n**Verification:** a fake-LLM run checked that the cached block is identical across the save round, its follow-up round, and the next turn, and across two dates. The test redirected the athlete and usage files to a temp directory, so `data/` and `logs/` were not touched.\n\n**Open risk:** caching only engages above 1,024 tokens for Sonnet 4.5. My estimate puts the new cached prefix right around that line, and I couldn't count tokens without calling the API. If it's under, nothing gets cached and every call costs full price. After deploying, check `logs/usage.jsonl`: a normal follow-up message should show `cache_read_input_tokens` near the static size. If every call shows 0 for both read and creation, add about 100 tokens of real stable content to the static block.\n\n**Not changed:** keyword-based tool selection changes the `tools` array, which is part of the cache prefix, so switching tool sets still misses the cache. NOTES.md calls that filter a clear win, 